[h1]HWMP Patch 2.4.5 - Cataclysm (Field Test)[/h1]
Standalone Homeworld Remastered multiplayer patch based on the complete Players Patch 2.3Test build21, retaining the original four races. Use this package by itself; do not stack another Players Patch. Every MP client needs the same Workshop revision.

[h2]Cataclysm: Support Units mode[/h2]
Choose [b]HWMP 2.4.5 Cataclysm[/b] under Game Type in skirmish/multiplayer. The existing Hiigaran, Vaygr, Kushan and Taiidan races use a shared weighted SU pool. Ordinary HWMP modes remain available.

[list]
[*] Nominal budgets: Small 1440; Normal 1920; Large 2560; Huge 3840; Vast 7680.
[*] SU prices in construction, tooltips and selected-ship descriptions; owned-fleet counter below Resource Units.
[*] Existing carrier/shipyard count caps remain; carriers add no capacity. Zero-SU probes keep classic caps.
[*] The HUD counts full configured squadron entries, including docked ones. Queued construction is excluded; surviving physical hulls are not measured.
[*] four original-race menu emblems
[*] Russian naming/encoding corrections
[/list]

[h2]Known SU limitation — please read[/h2]
[b]The SU limiter is currently unreliable.[/b]

Native accounting of small fractional ship weights differs from the displayed nominal prices. Some compositions are refused early; others can exceed the displayed budget. The size of the mismatch depends on fleet composition and is not necessarily small.

Native tests with the former 1900 budget reproduced ordinary-UI refusal at 1885 for a 15 SU order. Separate AI/backend tests completed paid construction to 1915/1900 even though every request first received CanBuild approval. The same overflow through the human UI, simultaneous producers, cancellations, replenishment, capture, saves/mode switching and two-client synchronization are not yet verified.

[b]This update changes ceilings to multiples of 32; it does not fix fractional ship-cost accounting.[/b]

Startup and readable SU UI have been checked on the preceding runtime. Source/Lua4 checks cover the new ceilings; no new native run of this ceiling revision is claimed. Full-match balance/stability remain field tests, without a crash-free guarantee.

[h2]Shared fixes[/h2]
[list]
[*] Owner-safe gravity restoration with specific tested new save/load cases;
[*] support-frigate cargo recovery;
[*] per-ship capture/self-destruct permissions;
[*] independent stalled-docking timers;
[*] refreshed Taiidan missile-defense targets;
[*] restored Vaygr Medium missile weapon-fire binding.
[*] Accepted Hiigaran/Vaygr6/6 collector starts,
[*] Accepted Assault Frigate final speed-accuracy multiplier 1.2
[*] Accepted two scoped missile corrections.
[*] Six native tooltip languages.
[*] Old active-well saves predating the journal are not guaranteed.
[/list]

Please report Game Type, Unit Cap, race, matching archive hashes, displayed SU, queue state, RU spent and reproducible actions.
Known limitations and current documentation:
